<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">328 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">328 CE in world history: 3 events, 2 deaths and 1 work. 142 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/23">23 CE</a><a href="/years/69">69 CE</a><a href="/years/224">224 CE</a><a href="/years/260">260 CE</a><a href="/years/328" aria-current="page">328 CE</a><a href="/years/357">357 CE</a><a href="/years/378">378 CE</a><a href="/years/392">392 CE</a><a href="/years/394">394 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/athanasius-of-alexandria" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/athanasius-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-9">9 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Athanasius is elected patriarch of Alexandria</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Alexandrian Council elected Athanasius to succeed Alexander as patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>. A leading defender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene Christianity</a>, he spent over 17 years in five exiles ordered by four different Roman emperors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athanasius-of-alexandria">Athanasius of Alexandria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/danube" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/danube.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-5">5 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Constantine's Bridge over the Danube is officially opened</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Constantine's Bridge, a Roman bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> between Sucidava in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a> and Oescus in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, built by the architect Theophilus Patricius, was officially opened. Used to reconquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dacia">Dacia</a>, it remained in use for four decades.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
